{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/788869-ways-to-recover-willpower","id":788869,"title":"Ways to Recover Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-18T11:03:51-08:00","id":788869,"title":"Ways to Recover Willpower","content":"So I'm putting together a list for my Werewolf players to know how to recover their Willpower. While scouring the book, I didn't find reference to a good night's sleep regaining 1 Willpower (at least not directly: the First Trimester Condition says you get <b>an additional</b> Willpower point with 4+ hours of sleep, and the Nightmare Plague Dread Power on page 222 says you don't get the willpower because of bad sleep). So now I'm totally at a loss as to all of the ways that a character can recover willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What I definitely know (using only Werewolf)<br /> Anchor stuff: Act in accordance with Virtue/Mask/Blood/Legend, or Vice/Dirge/Bone/Life. Interact with Touchstones.<br /> Resolve Inspired Condition.<br /> Surrender after being Beaten Down.<br /> Exceptional Success in Down &amp; Dirty Combat<br /> Have the First Trimester Condition, sleep more than 4 hours<br /> Exchange sweat with a Wolf-blooded with the Exciting Tell<br /> Get an exceptional success on the Dream Hunter Gibbous Moon Facet<br /> Spend an Essence when using the Barghest Facet against a corporeal undead target<br /> Exceptional Success on Lay Low the Challenger Facet<br /> Have the Destroyer Blood, be affected by the Kindle Fury Rite, indulge in Blood<br /> Participate in Harness the Cycle Rite<br /> <br /> That's all that I've found in the Werewolf book. I suspect that the only one that's missing is an explicit &quot;You get one back for sleeping.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 12-18-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T14:53:01-08:00","id":788973,"title":"","content":"It is one of the mortal rules and I'd personally say it still applies since you add the template of forsaken to a mortal and no where do I see it said that this general rule isn't present. <br /> <br /> <br /> But I could be wrong. Unlike a vampire though it is less thematically appropriate or expected but some still are divided on where vampires fall as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T15:18:04-08:0